      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I went hunting for a canny for this because we still need it. I still want to set my volume to default sometimes for world and other audio source testing. \n\nTo even figure out the \"true\" defaults I asked around my friend group and it was inconclusive! I waited until a friend had a new computer/operating system install and I had the forethought to ask her to send a screenshot of the default audio settings when she logged in for the first time on the new computer. It feels SO silly to go to these lengths to know this - when reset all could be right there with the reset other user's volume. \n\nThe attached picture shows the default audio levels from a new install of VRChat on a new computer/os (as of winter 2025). Hope it helps anyone reading on while we wait for a reset solution. (I have cropped her name for privacy, but Thank you!)\n\nWith that said I can't believe item/effects audio defaults to 100%. With it at that level the audio leaks out of my headphones and back out my microphone. Aaah. \n\nLet's get a \"reset to default\" here so people just can better know about these things.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
